<% layout('layouts/boilerplate') %>

<div class="container py-5">
  <div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-10">
      
      <!-- Page Header -->
      <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm rounded-4 p-4 p-md-5 mb-4 bg-white">
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <div class="ta-icon-wrapper icon-blue fs-3 mb-0">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-user-shield"></i>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="badge bg-primary-subtle text-primary rounded-pill px-3 py-1 fw-semibold small">Legal & Trust</span>
            <h1 class="fw-bold display-6 mb-0 mt-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0 fs-6">
          Learn how TravelAtlas handles user account data, community contributions, and platform privacy principles.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Content Card -->
      <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm rounded-4 p-4 p-md-5 bg-white">
        <div class="space-y-4">

          <section class="mb-4">
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info text-primary me-2"></i>1. Overview</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
              TravelAtlas is a community-driven travel knowledge platform where users explore and share factual destination guides. We value your privacy and are committed to maintaining a transparent environment for all community members.
            </p>
          </section>

          <hr class="my-4 text-light-subtle" />

          <section class="mb-4">
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-database text-info me-2"></i>2. Information We Collect</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-2">When you register or interact with TravelAtlas, we collect the following types of information:</p>
            <ul class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
              <li><strong>Account Credentials:</strong> Username, email address, bio, and optional profile image provided during account registration.</li>
              <li><strong>Community Contributions:</strong> Destination entries, reviews, star ratings, travel tips, parking availability metrics, crowd levels, and uploaded photos.</li>
              <li><strong>Technical Data:</strong> Basic request parameters (e.g. IP address for security rate-limiting and session management cookies).</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <hr class="my-4 text-light-subtle" />

          <section class="mb-4">
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-eye text-success me-2"></i>3. Public Content & Visibility</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
              TravelAtlas is designed as a public travel repository. Reviews, travel tips, ratings, and destination guides submitted by registered travelers are publicly visible to enable fellow travelers to make informed travel decisions. Your public username and profile picture are displayed alongside your contributions.
            </p>
          </section>

          <hr class="my-4 text-light-subtle" />

          <section class="mb-4">
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-lock text-warning me-2"></i>4. Security & Data Protection</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
              We employ standard application security measures, including salted password hashing via <code>Passport-Local-Mongoose</code>, NoSQL query sanitization, HTTP Content Security Policies (CSP), and rate-limiting middleware to protect account credentials from unauthorized access.
            </p>
          </section>

          <hr class="my-4 text-light-subtle" />

          <section class="mb-4">
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-minus text-danger me-2"></i>5. Account Deletion & Knowledge Preservation</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed">
              Users can delete their accounts at any time through their profile management dashboard. To maintain community knowledge integrity and prevent broken destination pages, contributed destination records and reviews remain preserved on the platform under an anonymized author moniker ("Anonymous Traveler") after account removal.
            </p>
          </section>

          <hr class="my-4 text-light-subtle" />

          <section>
            <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-headset text-purple me-2"></i>6. Contact Us</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-0">
              If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or TravelAtlas data practices, please reach out to our community team at <a href="mailto:privacy@travelatlas.com" class="text-decoration-none fw-semibold">privacy@travelatlas.com</a>.
            </p>
          </section>

        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>
